THE PAPER. 15 pages. Collapsed equality classes and quantitative selection for the Joukowsky boundary problem.

For J_r(z) = rz + 1/(rz) the elliptic boundary problem has a unique source maximizer when r > 1, namely normalized Haar measure on the circle. At r = 1 the ellipse collapses to the segment, the boundary map identifies reflected points, and the equality class becomes an infinite-dimensional affine fiber, described completely as d eta = (1+h) dm with h odd under conjugation and |h| <= 1. Reopening with r = e^s, every member of the collapsed fiber has first-order deficit converging to one half the squared L2 norm of h, so restoring injectivity selects Haar measure quantitatively from the collapsed class. The selection functional has sharp range from zero to one half. A finite-Blaschke corollary identifies which covered members remain maximizers at every nondegenerate scale.

